# Two tetrahedra (a b c d) and (a b c e) glued along their shared face
# a-b-c form a watertight triangular bipyramid (V=5 E=9 F=6). Faces
# 2 (a d b) and 4 (a b e) share edge a-b; d and e lie in the SAME plane
# z=0 on the same side of line a-b, so the triangles overlap past their
# common edge instead of folding away. Every face has nonzero area and
# every earlier face pair joins legitimately, so the witness is faces=2,4.
v a 0 0 0
v b 6 0 0
v c 0 0 5
v d 2 4 0
v e 4 3 0
f a c d
f a d b
f b d c
f a b e
f b c e
f c a e
